$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{6}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{6}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{6{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{|\\sqrt{6}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{6}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06349d8e-8391-574b-b6ee-d09717af159e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247480} {:answer/id #uuid "28b08c9d-77c7-5bea-8de3-24e47c4a6b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247786} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4c8ae4-b8b1-5ed2-b232-73c90f37ed26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248097} {:answer/id #uuid "97ffb8aa-ac92-5db2-a3d4-4a6b34576f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248778} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b1dd01-2ffe-53eb-9456-1dfad676593b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28b08c9d-77c7-5bea-8de3-24e47c4a6b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247786} :answer-field/id #uuid "f124bfeb-924c-5974-b5d6-5bac9d8b7458" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d978df6a-8484-5ed1-885e-b4758185514d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114056" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{8}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{8}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "243323f6-ad70-573c-a08a-406469d3a0ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247740} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7538ae-df96-5bd6-89c4-eb9b39dfc0b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247852} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf8e15f-3174-57fb-b8e4-5d360ff846f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248257} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8775a6-08c9-5e68-8ded-0ebea2805076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248846} {:answer/id #uuid "a3358706-6bfa-540b-8aac-27669d842b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bf8e15f-3174-57fb-b8e4-5d360ff846f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248257} :answer-field/id #uuid "6296fb51-a261-5315-98e2-bafc87eb4fd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4d360a8-fe79-5362-9972-fed2a1994303" :question/math-academy-id "q-114074" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd84a82-8cbc-585f-8bbe-ce19fdb09a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247954} {:answer/id #uuid "47871075-deb3-513b-8a8e-3639234f622c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248060} {:answer/id #uuid "983ebb92-bd83-5ed1-a0f3-8fe2c8c188ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248782} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c31917-04d7-582e-b1d4-e26865d402a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248917} {:answer/id #uuid "af0b67fe-7271-56c8-8367-495b25ff2f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c31917-04d7-582e-b1d4-e26865d402a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248917} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f9281c-e5d7-5f72-ac5c-0b25153c48f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8425d47-32c7-547c-ab87-ac1c6071e1e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114078" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/8)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012323fc-4e7b-5948-bd33-ac6535cdacea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247423} {:answer/id #uuid "275108dc-ba21-516f-8c42-bd8bf8d71064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247772} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab5218b-e36e-59ff-8b03-f71a3f5c4374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247944} {:answer/id #uuid "82b6c265-2f3d-5dbe-b622-87847517b9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248580} {:answer/id #uuid "afcf5a5d-6b1c-5e07-b91a-41eca607a863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcf5a5d-6b1c-5e07-b91a-41eca607a863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249002} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f84de4-1a81-5ce2-ac8e-5901c4a2a352" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c216ad6d-32f4-5235-ae6f-6f4e1e6db054" :question/math-academy-id "q-114080" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b573ef-1007-53ad-a1f4-f1bbb6a97f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247434} {:answer/id #uuid "21345a50-5601-54ac-b6b8-8854f3bcf25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247719} {:answer/id #uuid "21932059-2779-56bb-aff8-46d2133806aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247722} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ca1c00-7abb-53af-b061-a218e5f95af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249025} {:answer/id #uuid "fe379fad-f57a-50e1-ad28-7deffbfbf656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b573ef-1007-53ad-a1f4-f1bbb6a97f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247434} :answer-field/id #uuid "20529d1c-5c66-5379-87b8-bf5bcb3ca23c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d206bd2a-2b8b-589e-945a-46c1dd7ed6d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114084" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ace781-d274-5e56-a670-5a4a11cc396e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}^{3}\\text{ arcsin }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247581} {:answer/id #uuid "5692d53f-e590-5c4b-b3cf-b26aac77396a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248210} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc18efd-3204-5471-89ef-885c34415cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsin }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249128} {:answer/id #uuid "d2dad63e-a18d-5765-8de3-fdf0ca004d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}^{3}\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249295} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4b608f-ffe9-5210-b69f-f21778e1a218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-7\\text{ arctan }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5692d53f-e590-5c4b-b3cf-b26aac77396a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248210} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b1cbd54-3439-59c4-a3d8-a241f241223c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb0e1654-81f3-51ff-a1ad-22ecef08f60d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114164" :question/problem "$\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+7(\\text{ arcsec }x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263a6676-bcc6-56f2-bf75-5b204a0665c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247761} {:answer/id #uuid "8afc0f1b-1e0c-5d92-a062-0d61fc9caadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248663} {:answer/id #uuid "9369dced-f14b-556e-945e-9f6e682f7d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248734} {:answer/id #uuid "945bb0e9-9cf8-5d4f-a7ae-aab444d3de81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248744} {:answer/id #uuid "f074aa68-1eb8-5f6d-8644-d4e407e90daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f074aa68-1eb8-5f6d-8644-d4e407e90daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249535} :answer-field/id #uuid "916b2a0c-4759-5859-ac15-e71d9797d8fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca385184-ef23-5e09-850b-a334c3c5908a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114168" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(0-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250206 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9fbe19-cf60-531c-baf0-c504de2ac80c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247524} {:answer/id #uuid "19c56598-e8ce-5d22-8ffa-5f30dd11841a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247660} {:answer/id #uuid "57c92f5d-6664-5cf7-9fc7-0643b248d475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248221} {:answer/id #uuid "5d314c53-79f8-54f8-b84b-eae20722ae51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248272} {:answer/id #uuid "c6cc8340-3010-5529-9554-55c7d0dc7818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19c56598-e8ce-5d22-8ffa-5f30dd11841a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247660} :answer-field/id #uuid "366d90ae-e6be-58b7-a32f-61ddab4f0f9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "646baf8c-2fc5-5cdc-90e1-2b00b50de1be" :question/math-academy-id "q-114202" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{y}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}-3(-{y}^{-1}){|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2(-1-(-2))+3(\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{1}{(-2)}) \\\\  & =2(-1+2)+3(-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2(1)+3\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459929b5-16a5-5034-94f0-b9e58f15ceec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248048} {:answer/id #uuid "64343e0f-0dc4-59b1-9b42-e034415d89e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248328} {:answer/id #uuid "81c1316f-a38a-5e2e-b549-e63e68e66f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248573} {:answer/id #uuid "a9fe39d8-722a-5b08-a7b5-69095e8360bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248934} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7cabaa-8d3a-58ef-b215-67b7a26ae5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "459929b5-16a5-5034-94f0-b9e58f15ceec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248048} :answer-field/id #uuid "e640f0ef-8ce1-5b26-8c98-c9b2965485ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d22fa8db-1712-5866-9e2b-91e93589e8f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114245" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}^{′}}{{[{x}^{2}-2x+1]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}^{′}}{{[2x-2]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01827748-212d-560e-98f3-b45c7c8273e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247428} {:answer/id #uuid "124ecb28-d039-500b-a460-c817f5999b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247589} {:answer/id #uuid "954f57bf-be13-5e8b-bc74-e37ff744e3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248753} {:answer/id #uuid "a2878e25-4fd1-52ce-b0a3-685f50cbf8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248875} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1a3389-4f89-55ad-9187-e9cc38d950e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01827748-212d-560e-98f3-b45c7c8273e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247428} :answer-field/id #uuid "14fa5bf4-26c0-5e7f-8772-8b5826495a67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1490f312-92c6-56e8-8f14-6e1263bd40da" :question/math-academy-id "q-114249" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=-1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1]}^{′}}{{[{x}^{2}+2x+1]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)}{2x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)}{2x+2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)]}^{′}}{{[2x+2]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{x+2}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{1}{2(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26da406a-b1ee-533c-8e84-f3f3308fd3a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247767} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} {:answer/id #uuid "b96beb80-9254-5797-a25b-3e85eaa45af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{3{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249082} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8237c1-5f1b-5b27-84a1-36bf62527629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249105} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f75f10-d4ff-5f2b-8f08-23ed364814bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ddb17e-a21a-5bc8-bdfe-e5654290dd4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a75c4b14-7006-556e-bd1e-e4613f35b446" :question/math-academy-id "q-114287" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a625e0-f342-5d88-863b-2cc610f12c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x-1){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247918} {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} {:answer/id #uuid "4d558edc-f058-5d64-aa0f-acff177c0e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-3x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248117} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa27907-71bc-5690-9d5a-5ea98a3a03cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248503} {:answer/id #uuid "cd15176c-1580-5959-a4f3-0332eefaf817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2-x){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} :answer-field/id #uuid "f37b9f98-70f3-5724-8992-60b01c3a21f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1022e01f-7a5a-562e-a877-5ba5b3c9edd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114293" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x-4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x-4)\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x-4)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-3){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0251f12b-0bcd-5543-9eb5-f4ec7e4c9752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} {:answer/id #uuid "7229d8df-ae59-5660-b41e-cae11851e04c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248420} {:answer/id #uuid "91224b99-89c4-59ce-b789-19a10d61178d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248714} {:answer/id #uuid "dc01fc34-a583-577b-8fdc-401ef22073b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249369} {:answer/id #uuid "f20a32cf-99d1-5344-b1f0-7a8da3242cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0251f12b-0bcd-5543-9eb5-f4ec7e4c9752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec890aa8-f649-5040-b0db-08c864882cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de415510-24b2-53a0-b8c3-ddc9cdee62b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114294" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\right)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{3}⁡x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6729e761-a109-51c4-8606-18751a53f95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248350} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf1abf3-9f83-5499-84e8-2cdbf9e21301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248682} {:answer/id #uuid "aeaf0778-2cce-5ff4-8bd6-a8910cbdb116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248985} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e5714-4c05-5edb-b661-6e6122f8d589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7740ab9-c0ff-5f8c-91e3-87881adad76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a77892-fbcb-5fb9-802a-ce425028c881" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\right)\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3878ae79-1e5e-59bf-8bb6-ae0cf3aaa4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247928} {:answer/id #uuid "5f75b493-3947-527e-a588-60cab80d2be3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248287} {:answer/id #uuid "74e4c221-78c2-5702-af4f-442e99facd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248451} {:answer/id #uuid "cef45258-9cb1-562e-a7e4-faf62bbc7406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249259} {:answer/id #uuid "e0dd153a-e09b-5898-9188-70f04b5e8044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3878ae79-1e5e-59bf-8bb6-ae0cf3aaa4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247928} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b71088-363e-519b-b126-45df5c59e3e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40079a0f-e072-5ffd-a039-30e177ed76fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-114304" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d87cf2-ba4e-5ee2-b888-16334d204447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247661} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfa8fa7-c8a9-5491-a85f-a85434d1131e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247678} {:answer/id #uuid "5b42bf75-0d9b-5855-aac9-9999790d5338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248251} {:answer/id #uuid "a03cb483-a296-5946-8a8d-952eac55cad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248855} {:answer/id #uuid "aedb9126-7c6d-5c55-ad4b-869a319638e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d87cf2-ba4e-5ee2-b888-16334d204447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247661} :answer-field/id #uuid "0416b7bd-da37-58c6-8855-48ba00ca405e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edc6fd62-64ca-5ae7-b219-55728bf85a2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114306" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} {:answer/id #uuid "ab51dc5a-a926-51cd-8e7b-df0870f057c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248946} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cbad19-d246-5b98-8980-41bddf12f22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249448} {:answer/id #uuid "e99bc9d8-a545-56d1-baef-23123e5ae336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{6}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249486} {:answer/id #uuid "f8073886-20e6-5ba4-879b-63835b53eb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9a9941-4c05-5900-9e9e-c028b2cee8de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64685827-c31f-5450-80d9-3d65e9e828de" :question/math-academy-id "q-114309" :question/problem "$\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+4)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+4)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}\\right)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c09516b-ffde-5c4c-8dbe-564104924571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{15}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248513} {:answer/id #uuid "a581301a-72c3-5cfb-8ef1-56abefe481a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{25}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248900} {:answer/id #uuid "a5873c57-b416-5bd2-86d9-681f98615c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248901} {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ae0e29-77f1-5100-a586-609d2c797e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{15}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea192b1-985a-504b-a59a-fe45ed09d88a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d0e94f6-1e93-555f-a728-ca5181d50236" :question/math-academy-id "q-114312" :question/problem "$\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}\\right)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c3019c-5b9e-5399-b786-04437705e092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} {:answer/id #uuid "6f81ffd7-1892-5f9b-9320-925504438589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248407} {:answer/id #uuid "89d313a8-f000-577f-a816-a34a6622496f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248650} {:answer/id #uuid "a7092c76-1bc1-50c0-b6c7-d05f207eda48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248909} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f08285-93fd-5b63-ade9-e4f908688cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c3019c-5b9e-5399-b786-04437705e092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1b567b-6514-5d16-ba8c-83023f80f2da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "062977fc-037b-5a67-9a07-c0d038a63f3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114318" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)] \\\\  & =-[1-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771a4680-23b4-5532-bdca-e5e5e51c2e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248472} {:answer/id #uuid "788019d8-4726-57ee-8d3c-f8c472f663ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248481} {:answer/id #uuid "938dda6d-62d5-5932-8236-a8efaf7f79ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248736} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} {:answer/id #uuid "ac64494d-e051-58cd-912e-6906743c182e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc9c08d-e5e1-5b3f-9652-c2d450c9f225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ecbdeecb-1f0c-572b-8510-8e18414c1281" :question/math-academy-id "q-114320" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-2x} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}\\right)\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-2x}{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0{e}^{-2(0)}-(-1){e}^{-2(-1)}]-\\frac{3}{4}[{e}^{-2(0)}-{e}^{-2(-1)}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0+{e}^{2}]-\\frac{3}{4}[1-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d83e583-d218-50f4-abb7-474c6d01c304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247546} {:answer/id #uuid "3d047995-440b-51a6-837d-6a9c0a9dea33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247961} {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7776ae-27e1-5fb2-91d8-1d3d11b460fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248680} {:answer/id #uuid "aea67226-a698-5829-a7e0-c9089694e776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff430e6-479c-5fff-ae3c-19a79a5cfe3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37affd24-3b4f-536c-8927-723157249685" :question/math-academy-id "q-114328" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right)-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{9}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d8920c-9eae-5d0e-8971-ca7e7b55533e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e-3}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248477} {:answer/id #uuid "7b577e2d-1a9b-598e-a5bb-8e6d22918919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248506} {:answer/id #uuid "82f9258b-b72f-566d-a506-e8c7094ed4bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248582} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d80631-c8d5-5425-9e65-8029a411c1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249042} {:answer/id #uuid "fb407c98-f1d8-5183-b7e1-e23543be95c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{e+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4d80631-c8d5-5425-9e65-8029a411c1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249042} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf81a2af-d8b3-5358-9ec2-8ae5505c5bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e406eb1a-a97b-5da3-8a7a-44bb2a8c8ae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-114329" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}9x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=9x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=9 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 9x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =9x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)\\cdot 9\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-3x}+3\\int {e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}9x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-3x{e}^{-3x}{|}_{0}^{1/3}+3{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-3x}{|}_{0}^{1/3}-{e}^{-3x}{|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =-3[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3(1/3)}-0\\cdot {e}^{-3\\cdot 0}]-[{e}^{-3(1/3)}-{e}^{-3\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =-3[\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{3}-0]-[{e}^{-1}-1] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{e}-\\frac{1}{e}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e-2}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47329e42-9fda-5dad-b1b7-b5de92199ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248057} {:answer/id #uuid "584e2ce7-69ed-515b-b3d8-ae953f17271d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248225} {:answer/id #uuid "90842d88-2e12-51f4-925b-763cbdc1a0b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248708} {:answer/id #uuid "ad07dcb5-9bc9-5064-b6c1-d6071522fe76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248972} {:answer/id #uuid "df5f96e4-8268-56cf-9d0e-ec8e56b4e1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47329e42-9fda-5dad-b1b7-b5de92199ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248057} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7aa87d-cda1-557e-8fb5-e5baaeecced7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "447c75d4-22ec-5570-87c0-7a6b7bbeb6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114341" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(1,-5)$ and the line $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's draw a diagram describing our situation.  \n\n![](images/3a/3a4bbfd80480fe3fcc778a490514d27d65d83abf77ca1752e4203d9b3185b618.png)\n\nFirst, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3$ and passes through the point $(1,-5).$\n\nThe given line has a slope of $-\\frac{3}{2},$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+5 & =\\frac{2}{3}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{2}{3}-5 \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3 \\\\ y &=\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}x+3 & =\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{17}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{2}{3}x & =-\\frac{17}{3}-3 \\\\ -\\frac{13}{6}x & =-\\frac{26}{3} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{26}{3}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{6}{13}\\right) \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-3.$ So, our solution is $x=4$ and $y=-3.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(4,-3).$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(1,-5)$ and $(4,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4-1)^{2}+(-3+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(1,-5)$ and the line $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3$ is $\\sqrt{13}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029577c8-4387-5dce-abc1-e362769c0f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247442} {:answer/id #uuid "4e18de69-f618-587b-a2ec-5220370f7b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248124} {:answer/id #uuid "8d733b4b-1dca-53a4-a8f8-a44dd6bcbc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248683} {:answer/id #uuid "a03c6caa-d5e0-51d2-ab76-a5150a905444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248854} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf847c0-a882-5640-8efa-f13f377ac775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a03c6caa-d5e0-51d2-ab76-a5150a905444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248854} :answer-field/id #uuid "e155ce82-9147-55f3-82af-e32fec80f54d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "590fb4d1-46ef-5eb8-ba9c-0c9e6a8189ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-114429" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)] \\\\  & =-[2-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a05c2fc-f94d-5489-955e-6e93003cb216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\pi -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247662} {:answer/id #uuid "a3dc3121-d85d-555d-95fa-e1f130a553c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248887} {:answer/id #uuid "a75bb911-b1a2-59de-ac5b-2d5b63e7d0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248911} {:answer/id #uuid "c53da061-88b8-5d38-9620-69fbe5f388d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249176} {:answer/id #uuid "e1bfdf52-8608-5e41-81ac-9c0e93199b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a75bb911-b1a2-59de-ac5b-2d5b63e7d0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248911} :answer-field/id #uuid "a980c72c-15a0-5296-ad73-7e85baf7f354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3841fdbd-8341-5e24-9f59-0d6b99ab3106" :question/math-academy-id "q-114441" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =[-0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c892137-db18-57ab-a0c4-ee121e607cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247538} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2a7067-db8e-5098-bfe6-d1f90479e95e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248104} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0a2abd-f164-5bc3-8dd3-b337d3b3b315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248389} {:answer/id #uuid "ad009786-2f7e-5893-ae43-3dd8c76182ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248969} {:answer/id #uuid "f843f5bd-ea3e-5dce-a8a3-d0d60b0e0281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c892137-db18-57ab-a0c4-ee121e607cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f0563b6-4107-5961-bf6f-8fdb92fa27b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ae308dc-8f77-58de-a2c1-ae20d02ecf13" :question/math-academy-id "q-114454" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2{csc}^{2}⁡x+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{x}^{3}){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+{\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)}^{3}-[-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)+{\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)}^{3}] \\\\  & =-0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}+2(1)-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{64} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3558fbac-1b59-57fe-9bd0-f677f28f907a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247904} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbae598-1c6b-5eca-9ed6-66dceae7fb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248275} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8c8c5c-01b7-553f-b6a2-1e3b22313e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248700} {:answer/id #uuid "d23ea027-eba2-500a-9470-4d37e94b1732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249290} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f3cf69-d025-571c-b710-5dfbc6ea9479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dbae598-1c6b-5eca-9ed6-66dceae7fb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9fe6922-c9ab-5e3a-bc26-b2f81f8df27d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dcffc55-70b6-5a56-9948-97e923b1fff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114460" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51767ce2-04dc-5c92-be64-ecdd456e4d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248156} {:answer/id #uuid "5af05724-0a68-584c-bdcc-e0f997546e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248248} {:answer/id #uuid "a32c58bd-145a-53ec-98dc-145783470c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248884} {:answer/id #uuid "b0502d42-a25a-5ae1-9cca-dcf3a4cbe860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249008} {:answer/id #uuid "c64da03c-c464-59cb-81c9-d62f5d957afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0502d42-a25a-5ae1-9cca-dcf3a4cbe860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249008} :answer-field/id #uuid "a22fa253-1174-584a-9758-f3f964e75c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91292256-4f82-5669-95d9-e91e8b8d6af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114552" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\ {v}^{′}=2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(x)({x}^{2})-\\int ({x}^{2})\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{5}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aec5f05-d22a-5c56-9672-60bc96c1bb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247519} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5abc59-c7e4-5c8a-87f4-b54b803742a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247702} {:answer/id #uuid "35fbcfa4-611f-5481-a5a0-e26daf32fe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247912} {:answer/id #uuid "3e70e2aa-5270-59bd-8d76-329cce6e0fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247976} {:answer/id #uuid "e913e7e7-7377-58f1-a576-f2631769debf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e70e2aa-5270-59bd-8d76-329cce6e0fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247976} :answer-field/id #uuid "258426ca-e1eb-5f21-b193-8a88f0107073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ce30fbb-1b42-559b-a553-f2eb05e4f3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114553" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7ca2da-40f3-525c-bac6-b29d8480b2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247986} {:answer/id #uuid "a01808c9-616c-59db-89e8-974a2c400333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248852} {:answer/id #uuid "a30f743d-6b32-58c9-9c9b-527c9b8b888a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248883} {:answer/id #uuid "d8eb64cc-1ef2-5428-8c6b-e34b4c97b8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249336} {:answer/id #uuid "f65d4aa5-8ff1-5c46-aa50-cef0172e5477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a01808c9-616c-59db-89e8-974a2c400333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248852} :answer-field/id #uuid "80448976-ae2f-5f8d-b8a1-8ddcc578dda8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67ee7e99-c327-5643-bad9-04c09862c4b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114556" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\left(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\right)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3338599f-b719-52ec-a42e-1f9c762d4c09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1}{4{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247888} {:answer/id #uuid "9288729a-479e-5f0e-bb35-c0412ffb64f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248722} {:answer/id #uuid "b81fbb46-c0b8-52df-89da-8305c352443c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249071} {:answer/id #uuid "bb709158-d5c8-5b00-909d-3944db2f645c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249097} {:answer/id #uuid "ff12fe3e-1160-52e7-95f0-ea194932f43e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3}{{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb709158-d5c8-5b00-909d-3944db2f645c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249097} :answer-field/id #uuid "18a5e92e-4b0f-5381-bbbe-52226a63a592" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "362beb84-a4c5-596a-b73b-e0ca0f79f0fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-114557" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32c442b7-5812-5b9f-b5a3-9735de7bc5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247886} {:answer/id #uuid "a66e4f08-82a7-51c7-9f0f-a316a7a82095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248906} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1079b7-6c59-5146-a689-43939b214e55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248935} {:answer/id #uuid "c95f1123-d58f-569d-9f99-fc047c8ff23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249216} {:answer/id #uuid "fd5f9c6f-c38f-5d5f-aa01-a433d15de579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32c442b7-5812-5b9f-b5a3-9735de7bc5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247886} :answer-field/id #uuid "260a912a-e53c-57b3-a2f5-20d936d8b8f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "805d5bf3-56e5-56a7-8a77-c98eb5fe1df0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114585" :question/problem "$\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{2x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $2x+1=u,$ thus $2x=u-1$ and $\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\left(\\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{u-1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\,\\text{d}u+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{u}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡u}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{2x+1}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22097ee6-e029-5705-bd0d-12e8438e427a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247726} {:answer/id #uuid "3476300f-6f10-58d8-810a-76e72b26a106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247896} {:answer/id #uuid "46189a0d-05b3-5b4d-b076-027b366be2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248051} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0a2c8c-0d41-5bdb-b6b2-87f65ad145c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248498} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5f4ac2-3246-5235-8484-0b0f64f2b358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe5f4ac2-3246-5235-8484-0b0f64f2b358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249649} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7889684-8ec7-5297-81fb-c1d9b326d8d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5747f9d-1d5b-5a68-8df4-e21d4a5aef56" :question/math-academy-id "q-114597" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x){|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}x\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-x{|}_{1/3}^{e}\\, \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-(e-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+e-e+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06210c65-cc7a-5e4b-bf69-5482048cc94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247478} {:answer/id #uuid "1f8b6629-4046-5093-b11c-2c9ff8c296aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247704} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4a0cff-9e96-5852-b237-667134b904ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248828} {:answer/id #uuid "ade0ab9f-b410-5ccc-93ed-690c6b0b905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248978} {:answer/id #uuid "e484aeb9-9230-52f5-85a4-d8f264a2ce27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06210c65-cc7a-5e4b-bf69-5482048cc94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247478} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcabde0a-e8f2-56da-b3be-7871c9bb28e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16bb2470-b172-54fa-bb93-68ffa12f7218" :question/math-academy-id "q-114677" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16bd605d-4c29-506c-8ce7-c84c48b67fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247627} {:answer/id #uuid "34bd43f9-d4db-533f-acd2-5f7163057588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247897} {:answer/id #uuid "481e05e7-b62d-5851-a787-6a5d10613a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248068} {:answer/id #uuid "8e50b12e-9d6e-5a6e-8673-a420a275d68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248690} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5b9509-017e-5608-ad72-0fc4c95ad848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "481e05e7-b62d-5851-a787-6a5d10613a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248068} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2a0c2c0-21f1-56dd-ac06-3f6bd57cc988" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91699790-f225-57ae-8ea8-89f90b88a5ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-114679" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv{|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x){|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}x\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot 1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-x{|}_{1/2}^{1}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0-(1-\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "415bbc44-7f4c-58ad-8157-8f1f5ed47aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248005} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa4b914-459a-50f8-b61f-f8f5e3451572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248290} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc36f50-7f15-5f26-a2a4-236f583e6504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248521} {:answer/id #uuid "9025b8d7-d7e0-5ff3-b795-bc80c1e96b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248704} {:answer/id #uuid "b3394b3f-3533-568a-a273-e5b8ffd20f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "415bbc44-7f4c-58ad-8157-8f1f5ed47aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248005} :answer-field/id #uuid "01fbb077-6af9-5c0d-a4c5-a794f5a7f75d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ba36d0b-ab92-5237-aa17-794cfb598845" :question/math-academy-id "q-114681" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5x}{2}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5x}{2}\\right)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{5x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5x}{2}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5x}{2}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5x}{2}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5x}{2}\\right)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x]}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot [0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "056d0b62-18e9-55f0-8775-8042d2ae824c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{2}+4x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247469} {:answer/id #uuid "4a24ad98-a0b5-5cc3-a600-8812772a324b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-2x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248085} {:answer/id #uuid "75795d17-a5ee-582f-9b9e-c0ff0d8637fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248456} {:answer/id #uuid "ab67a9b5-9a63-5859-b7bb-9c8da59f41ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248948} {:answer/id #uuid "beb86753-1823-5658-bf1a-e594d3c2bfcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}({x}^{2}-2x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab67a9b5-9a63-5859-b7bb-9c8da59f41ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248948} :answer-field/id #uuid "8047459c-94d3-55f6-8eca-48002be93179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1074dd87-580f-51cd-9b83-51cf6a648213" :question/math-academy-id "q-114693" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4{x}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+1)\\left(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\right)(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}{2}-4\\int x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\left(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\right)(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(2x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}{2}-4(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(2x-1)+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}{2}-{e}^{2x}(2x-1)-4D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-4x+3)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-4D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189f9213-0590-5763-b7f1-5a9ff40545ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247646} {:answer/id #uuid "303bff0b-8c8d-570e-932f-08f4f7631376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247859} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec7d7a9-63ea-5dcf-a82f-7b1c3d305145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248132} {:answer/id #uuid "5779c8af-d348-5133-a80a-b74659af00bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248217} {:answer/id #uuid "df03a416-02ac-502d-9685-963bd71eb91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5779c8af-d348-5133-a80a-b74659af00bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248217} :answer-field/id #uuid "a867ef71-90c3-5a94-8b9a-8d5a238e8997" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4cfdf230-d427-5945-b883-cca5a7c6a112" :question/math-academy-id "q-114698" :question/problem "$\\int {cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc23f83-d209-56fe-ba9f-4d4ea28149d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247528} {:answer/id #uuid "347405c1-4237-56c7-8c18-11e44217feec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247895} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7e723e-dbfd-5048-8cdb-9b45ca1d33f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247987} {:answer/id #uuid "d0824483-e541-59f6-a789-31210d1c98a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}(4{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249273} {:answer/id #uuid "e68c2af6-fc8e-55c4-a7ed-0bca24c425da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(2{x}^{2}+x+4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "347405c1-4237-56c7-8c18-11e44217feec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247895} :answer-field/id #uuid "45b20a23-0102-5d8b-a89a-d0ed94ee9a91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c03c84f2-a54b-5cd7-81f9-a3bec98efab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114699" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=1-2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(1-2{x}^{2})\\left(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}\\right)(-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\left(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}\\right)(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C) \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56b4881f-232b-5196-af35-aea7cb58e62b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248212} {:answer/id #uuid "5968f717-2e1f-500b-b4d7-ccdd473f65be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248233} {:answer/id #uuid "60480242-e3f6-5bd4-97c9-e03d8a634da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248296} {:answer/id #uuid "75629651-ad7e-5b79-a799-0589d593b3ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248455} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa029d1-b400-582d-911d-327f96487132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60480242-e3f6-5bd4-97c9-e03d8a634da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248296} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b0fcafe-3643-59b7-8506-b7d096e4d110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "638cdd8d-a193-51d5-8d07-1c091b8aea29" :question/math-academy-id "q-114709" :question/problem "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8e6af2-4d5c-5c2a-a223-b1581d70cf90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247539} {:answer/id #uuid "81d0e0bb-c0c1-5d45-a394-2bbf8970a683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248575} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8ed56a-5c7f-5ef2-81bb-dd4b2068da0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248685} {:answer/id #uuid "b663df30-c9cb-50e7-be06-34aabcf17e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249056} {:answer/id #uuid "ec862b5c-e91d-5ccc-9ab8-a560591305a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec862b5c-e91d-5ccc-9ab8-a560591305a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249501} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fd4bc8-95db-5454-a58a-0b3490f1540b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f620a8f2-ded3-5ab5-a180-a9e0b77ecbff" :question/math-academy-id "q-114712" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f54fcd2-11eb-5de2-b3f7-146de7b6348a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}+2{log}_{4}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247564} {:answer/id #uuid "407f3c19-f6db-5e87-b664-92774974ae3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({log}_{4}⁡(x)+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247993} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0cac64-7a75-5a03-b08a-cee4bcbfa551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248695} {:answer/id #uuid "d24d95fe-f787-520e-9b19-d413da18936f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249291} {:answer/id #uuid "e86cde0d-e490-5e48-8a63-d7e0865c34b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e86cde0d-e490-5e48-8a63-d7e0865c34b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249477} :answer-field/id #uuid "e420d51c-8836-5780-9cc3-1975930de065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40de2008-379c-588d-bf38-59107f150b43" :question/math-academy-id "q-114880" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{4}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0566e525-d41b-5762-abad-a35a60fcea73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9e+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247468} {:answer/id #uuid "377a31ef-b562-5a6f-805e-2834d145cfda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247923} {:answer/id #uuid "928f1290-d85e-54cd-bd20-3cfebd037b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248724} {:answer/id #uuid "db06656d-5fcf-5439-bdb0-133473765928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249358} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ff3e4b-d499-52d7-802f-f1d97113fff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ff3e4b-d499-52d7-802f-f1d97113fff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249564} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddcf16bb-2de3-57be-904f-fe6f88d0b63a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25b1fd19-3728-5b2c-98ff-e3d6d85297ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-114883" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{3}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D) \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[e{ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{3})-6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})+18e]-[(1){ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{3})-6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})+18(1)] \\\\  & =9e-18e+18e-18 \\\\  & =9e-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bbba15-3ca2-548d-aa0b-fa8fde96be41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{13}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247648} {:answer/id #uuid "505545e5-5b59-5235-b0a9-6bfde088dc5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248143} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1c7d6f-7d36-5780-986c-93149710dad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248533} {:answer/id #uuid "7e81ded9-2f3b-592a-8788-962d13bc36f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248537} {:answer/id #uuid "abfdae4f-4dff-5106-9d49-8bae29e9c2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abfdae4f-4dff-5106-9d49-8bae29e9c2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248954} :answer-field/id #uuid "a24575db-05cf-5008-adac-d417701d5102" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "759dad06-62ad-59d4-9d65-70a46d8005a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114892" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 3 & -4 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & 3 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} & =3-\\frac{\\left(\\frac{17}{2}\\right)}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{17}{2x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[3x-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3(2-0)-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(2)+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(0)+3|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)] \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250316 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09d2a00f-4a5e-50ec-95a7-3d34717ca878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}[3-11\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247508} {:answer/id #uuid "4193cca1-11ab-5816-befe-e6e7082fd2b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}[1-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248007} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff3945d-cc27-5c31-8969-8fc40195197f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}[4-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248409} {:answer/id #uuid "94b6c9b3-1db7-55a8-8ada-45bd1cf3adf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248746} {:answer/id #uuid "ca649297-0c30-5fd0-a460-252be27d14b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}[17-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b6c9b3-1db7-55a8-8ada-45bd1cf3adf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248746} :answer-field/id #uuid "e407e99d-a50c-5c35-b3e1-dbdcca77665b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf68c363-607b-5ed8-bb76-a69145831fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-114894" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3(x-\\frac{1}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 2 & 5 \\\\  & ↓ & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+5}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})} & =2+\\frac{\\left(\\frac{17}{3}\\right)}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{17}{3(x-\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{17}{3x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(2+\\frac{17}{3x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\text{d}x+17{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[2x+\\frac{17}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(0-(-1))+\\frac{17}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3(0)-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3(-1)-1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(1)+\\frac{17}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2-\\frac{17}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2-\\frac{34}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9826cc-221a-58f0-a949-003259d10830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247516} {:answer/id #uuid "1935d4e4-d30d-5335-ab50-3b3fa04366e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(1+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247651} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9aeadf-fded-5a2b-861d-58af4c73c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247959} {:answer/id #uuid "54ac800d-c455-530d-b963-3aea2be7c145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248185} {:answer/id #uuid "6b902fe9-3b07-57e2-870c-2a793e643e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b902fe9-3b07-57e2-870c-2a793e643e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3226bde-c895-54e8-98cf-b5b2df79f6fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "462b058c-0216-5b9a-aa39-6bb6d7bc768e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114896" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $6$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & 2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} & =2+\\frac{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{4}{6x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}(2+\\frac{4}{6x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{4}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(0-\\left(-\\frac{1}{12}\\right))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(0)+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6\\left(-\\frac{1}{12}\\right)+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2\\left(\\frac{1}{12}\\right)+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b73f700-d96a-599b-ab52-2db5d3386e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247811} {:answer/id #uuid "3bfc4874-a112-5f03-a9d1-39829d4222c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[2-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247956} {:answer/id #uuid "4924bf57-6609-582a-b504-14c54c2c2e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248075} {:answer/id #uuid "55342b69-6990-55a7-b6b9-79464a3e57e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248192} {:answer/id #uuid "9991218e-5d69-54aa-88aa-8ca966e8ab5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4924bf57-6609-582a-b504-14c54c2c2e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248075} :answer-field/id #uuid "4388d5da-7f71-581a-8f21-f145c319a5de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e67ca108-b4a2-50be-81c1-fe32c84586b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114898" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 8 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 \\\\  & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} & =8+\\frac{3}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =8+\\frac{12}{4x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}(8+\\frac{12}{4x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\text{d}x+12{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-1|]_{-1/8}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8(0-\\left(-\\frac{1}{8}\\right))+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4(0)-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4\\left(-\\frac{1}{8}\\right)-1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082f5ffa-db8f-5b86-9f1f-66bec8888277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247495} {:answer/id #uuid "312a7284-86a2-58d1-925a-aae469b9cc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}+2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247869} {:answer/id #uuid "4646f294-569b-5c9a-8e3f-8b4bffc32dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-2e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248052} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1ab61f-f876-54ff-ac9a-719572398e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248654} {:answer/id #uuid "aed8ce21-2fef-51ea-932a-bf3d76234eac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a1ab61f-f876-54ff-ac9a-719572398e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248654} :answer-field/id #uuid "90297971-15bc-5633-a065-ce4100255f03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dca36867-5a6f-51bd-9e64-ad043dde12a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114900" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}(2{x}^{2})-\\int (2{x}^{2})\\left(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int x{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡x)\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$ \n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+1)-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2-2+1)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0188c738-8d3f-5f42-b61d-b6905e5bfdd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247429} {:answer/id #uuid "3788c026-240f-51ce-96e4-36b327b09c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247924} {:answer/id #uuid "52b4f6b7-1404-5c2e-b939-52278a731f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-3}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248167} {:answer/id #uuid "7654b839-b02e-5d72-8ce8-e1293aaa3cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248466} {:answer/id #uuid "b5aaf4ce-721d-5f9e-8dc0-70a1acafef73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5aaf4ce-721d-5f9e-8dc0-70a1acafef73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249050} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8f6cff-c895-5917-993d-b2d120420f39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c6784ae-fdbb-5b66-87d7-0cf88bfc85a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114910" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+18 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+18 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+18 \\\\  & =(x-3)^{2}+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-3)/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\left(\\frac{x-3}{3}\\right).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-3}{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-3)/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-3}{3}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
